    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74-a2">

                <pb facs="0230" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg102"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Duke to Mr.
                            Whitehouse</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 14,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I inform you that, according to a telegram from President Zaldivar, peace has
                    been arranged between this Republic and that of Guatemala, conceding a full
                    amnesty to all persons who took part in the revolution promoted by the decree of
                    General Barrios concerning the Central American Union. Representatives of the
                    five Republics will unite, shortly at Acajutla to fix the basis of the final
                    settlement of the difficulties pending, and until this takes place, the treaty
                    of friendship which existed before the war between Salvador and Guatemala
                    remains in force.</p>
                <closer><signed>J. MAURICE DUKE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
